AP64350 input hot-plug transient - does the SMBJ12A TVS help?
* Behavioural check only: cable inductance rings against the input capacitor when
* the 2S pack is plugged in. TVS is modelled as a zener (BV 13.3 V, SMBJ12A
* breakdown range 13.3-14.7 V); this is not a surge-standard qualification.
.param LCABLE=5u
.param RCABLE=50m
.param CIN=20u
.param VPK=8.4

* --- source: pack connected at 10 us ---
V1  src 0 PWL(0 0 10u 0 10.05u {VPK} 200u {VPK})
LC  src vin {LCABLE}
RC  vin vc {RCABLE}
CIN vc 0 {CIN}

* --- optional TVS: set USE_TVS=1 to include it ---
.param USE_TVS=1
*DTVS 0 vc DTVS
.model DTVS D(BV=13.3 IBV=1m RS=0.2 CJO=1n)

.tran 0.05u 200u
.meas tran vin_max MAX V(vc) FROM=10u TO=120u
.meas tran vin_min MIN V(vc) FROM=10u TO=120u
.meas tran vin_settled AVG V(vc) FROM=150u TO=190u
.end

